<p style="text-align: center;">Late Summer. 5x7, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">This is a small painting I did at the studio in Ballard from a reference photo that I took at a plein air painting location in Virginia. Working at this size is great for finding ways to simplify the landscape and use more expressive paint handling.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Spring has finally arrived in the Pacific Northwest after a rainy couple of months. My wife and I have moved into our new home in Seattle's Magnolia neighborhood, and my new studio in the basement is just about ready to start painting in (pics to follow).</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">While the new studio is a little smaller than the one I had in Virginia, I now have my own studio kitchen/office, as well as a bathroom, storage room and den. I'm excited to get back to work after taking a break for a couple of weeks while we moved.</p>
